      "id": 103,
      "student_id": 4,
      "title": "Student Project Showcase Portal",
      "description": "The Student Project Showcase Portal is a full-stack web application designed to provide a centralized platform where university students can showcase their academic and personal software projects while allowing recruiters to discover talented students and connect with them.\r\n\r\nThe application uses Google OAuth authentication for secure and seamless login. Students can create, edit, delete, and manage their project portfolios, including uploading project thumbnails, descriptions, technologies used, GitHub repository links, live demo links, and project categories. Recruiters can browse projects using advanced search and filtering, like projects, follow student profiles, and view complete project details.\r\n\r\nThe system follows a modern three-tier architecture consisting of a React frontend, a Node.js and Express backend REST API, and a MySQL relational database. Authentication is implemented using Google OAuth and JWT-based session management. Images are stored securely, and RESTful APIs handle communication between the frontend and backend.",
      "technology_stack": [
        "React",
        "Node.js",
        "Express.js",
        "MySQL",
        "Tailwind CSS"
      ],
